%% title: Request Lifecycle — openbank-api-gateway (Kong OSS 3.7.1 passthrough)
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Received : TCP connection accepted on :8000

    Received --> RouteMatching : HTTP request parsed

    RouteMatching --> BusinessRoute : path matches /api/v1/<resource>
    RouteMatching --> HealthRoute : path matches /health/<service>/*
    RouteMatching --> Rejected : no route matched

    BusinessRoute --> HeaderForwarding : route found (strip_path=false)
    HeaderForwarding --> Proxying : Authorization + X-Request-Id +\nX-Correlation-Id forwarded verbatim

    HealthRoute --> PathStripping : strip_path=true\n/health/account → /q/health
    PathStripping --> Proxying

    Proxying --> RetryLogic : upstream connect/read/write
    RetryLogic --> Proxying : retry attempt (max 2)
    RetryLogic --> UpstreamError : retries exhausted

    Proxying --> UpstreamResponse : upstream replies

    UpstreamResponse --> ResponseRelay : stream response back to client
    UpstreamError --> ResponseRelay : 502/503 gateway error

    Rejected --> ResponseRelay : 404 Not Found

    ResponseRelay --> AccessLogged : method, path, status, latency\nlogged to stdout (no body, no auth header)
    AccessLogged --> [*]

    note right of HeaderForwarding
        Kong does NOT inspect or validate JWT.
        Keycloak OIDC validation is done
        by the downstream Quarkus service.
    end note

    note right of Proxying
        connect_timeout: 5 000 ms
        write_timeout:  30 000 ms
        read_timeout:   30 000 ms
    end note
